Namespace-scope typedef of a qualified member type of a class-template instance
(`typedef std::vector<int>::iterator iter_t;`).  N5008 [temp.inst]/2,
[basic.lookup.qual], [temp.point].  Naming the member instantiates vector<int>,
which at C++20 elaborates its reverse_iterator member and the iterator-concept /
std::ranges::swap CPO chain for __normal_iterator; in the namespace-scope
qualified-name resolution context that evaluation raises an uncontained failure
that aborts resolution (the typedef is never created), while the same use inside
a function body and a namespace-scope vector<int> variable both succeed.  Same
family as std::string s("ab") (the concept chain truncates basic_string).
Reclassify to CORE when fixed.
See doc/architectural/cpp-class-template-instantiation-plan.md.
